{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/470", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"X.org 6.8.1 mouse cursor on Fooware MV1005 vid. chipset - is misshapen\", \"response\": \"If you are experiencing a misshapen mouse cursor in X.org version 6.8.1 with a Fooware MV1005 video chipset, it is likely due to a compatibility issue between the X.org server and the video chipset. This issue can be caused by a lack of support for the particular video chipset in the X.org server, or by a bug in the server's handling of the chipset.\\n\\nTo resolve this issue, you can try updating the X.org server to a newer version, if available, or try using a different window manager or desktop environment that may have better compatibility with your video chipset. You can also try using a different mouse cursor theme to see if that resolves the issue.\\n\\nAdditionally, you can try installing the proprietary drivers provided by Fooware for the MV1005 chipset, if available, as these drivers may provide better support for the chipset and resolve the issue with the misshapen mouse cursor.\\n\\nIf you are unable to resolve the issue with these steps, you may need to contact the developers of X.org or Fooware for further assistance.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/977", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What are the advantages for being in flow state\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nFlow state is a highly productive mental state, in which people report a deep sense of meaning, purpose, and effectiveness in their activities. Research has found that people in flow are much more productive and engaged in their work, and also report higher well-being and enjoyment of life. So flow state can be extremely beneficial for people who are able to reach it!\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nAre there any good practices for getting into flow state?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThere are several practices that have been shown to promote flow state. For example, you can use a “trigger” or activity to activate flow state, such as meditation, physical exercise, or deep focus on a task. Then you can try to remove any barriers to flow, such as removing distractions or making sure you have adequate time to complete a task. Finally, you can try to sustain your flow by keeping your mind focused on the task at hand. These practices can help you reach flow state more easily, and once you reach it, you can try to maintain it for as long as possible.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat is a good trigger for flow state?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nA good trigger for flow state can be anything that you find enjoyable or stimulating, such as reading a book, listening to music, playing a game, or doing physical exercise. You can also use a “flow trigger”, which is a specific activity or state of mind that has been shown to be particularly effective at promoting flow state. For example, some people like to use a “Five-Minute Flow” exercise, which involves sitting quietly and focusing on their breathing for five minutes, then trying to do something creative or productive. Another common flow trigger is listening to music while working on a task.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat are the benefits to flow coaching?\", \"response\": \"Flow coaching is a type of coaching that focuses on helping people reach and maintain flow state. Flow coaching can be beneficial for a number of reasons. First, it can help people become more productive and engaged in their work. Flow state is a highly productive mental state, in which people report a deep sense of meaning, purpose, and effectiveness in their activities. By helping people reach flow state, flow coaching can help them become more productive and engaged in their work.\\n \\n\\n Second, flow coaching can help people improve their well-being and enjoyment of life. People in flow state report higher well-being and enjoyment of life, so flow coaching can help people improve their overall quality of life.\\n \\n\\n Third, flow coaching can help people develop new skills and abilities. Flow state is a state of deep focus and concentration, in which people are able to learn and master new skills more quickly. By helping people reach flow state, flow coaching can help them develop new skills and abilities.\\n \\n\\n Overall, flow coaching can be a powerful tool for helping people reach their full potential and improve their lives.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/946", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Give me words that mean culture in languages that originate in Africa\\n \\n\\n give me words that mean “ culture” in their relative language not words about the cultures\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThere are many African languages that have words for culture, including Igbo omume, Yoruba asabe, Swahili ujumbe, and Twi afi.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nexplain the nuances for each\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe Igbo word omume can be translated as “culture”, and is often used to refer to cultural traditions, social customs, or ways of life. The Yoruba word asabe refers to the collective cultural beliefs, traditions, and practices of a particular group, and is often used to refer to culture in a broad sense. The Swahili word ujumbe refers to cultural traditions and practices, and is often used to refer to African culture in general. The Twi word afi refers to cultural values and traditions, and is often used to refer to traditional African culture.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nGive me words that mean ”creation” in languages that originate in Africa\\n \\n\\n give me words that mean “ creation” in their relative language not words about the cultures\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThere are many African languages that have words for creation, including Igbo ife, Yoruba aje, Swahili ujima, and Twi afi.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nexplain the nuances for each\", \"response\": \"The Igbo word ife means \\\"the act of bringing something into existence\\\" or \\\"the process of creating something new\\\". It is often used in the context of creating something tangible, such as a work of art, a new product, or a new idea.\\n \\n\\n The Yoruba word aje has a similar meaning to ife, and refers to the act of creating or bringing something into existence. It can also refer to the power or force behind creation.\\n \\n\\n The Swahili word ujima means \\\"the act of creating or making something\\\" or \\\"the process of bringing something into existence\\\". It can also refer to the act of creating a new society or community.\\n \\n\\n The Twi word afi has a similar meaning to ujima, and refers to the act of creating or making something. It can also refer to the idea of creating a new culture or tradition.\\n \\n\\n Overall, these words for creation in African languages capture the idea of bringing something new into existence, whether it be a physical object, a new idea, or a new cultural tradition.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/618", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"My wife and I separated several months ago and don't talk much.  It was her decision to move out, but I wanted to work on things.  Our anniversary is coming up soon.  Should I send her a gift or a note?  Can you write a short note for me?\", \"response\": \"I'm sorry to hear that you and your wife are going through a difficult time. It's understandable that you want to show her that you care, especially on your anniversary. Here are some thoughts and suggestions:\\n\\n1. Consider your wife's feelings and preferences: Before deciding whether to send a gift or a note, consider your wife's feelings and preferences. If she's not open to communicating with you or reconciliation is not a possibility, sending a gift or note may not be appropriate. It's important to respect her boundaries and wishes.\\n\\n2. If you decide to send a gift or note: If you decide to send a gift or note, keep it simple and thoughtful. A card with a heartfelt message expressing your love and appreciation for her could be a nice gesture. Here's an example of what you could write in a short note:\\n\\n\\\"Dear [Wife's Name],\\n\\nOur anniversary is a special day that reminds me of the love and joy we've shared together. Even though we're going through a difficult time right now, I want you to know that my love and appreciation for you remains unwavering. I hope this day is filled with happiness and memories for you, and I wish you all the best for the future.\\n\\nWith love,\\n[Your Name]\\\"\\n\\n3. Be mindful of the timing: It's important to be mindful of the timing of when you send the gift or note. Avoid sending it on the same day that she moved out or during a particularly difficult time for her. Instead, choose a time when she may be feeling more open and receptive to your gesture.\\n\\nRemember, the most important thing is to respect your wife's feelings and wishes, and to prioritize your own emotional well-being during this difficult time. Take care of yourself, and seek support from friends, family, or a therapist if needed.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/639", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"what are the objectives of shah waliullah ?\", \"response\": \"Shah Waliullah was a prominent Islamic scholar and theologian who lived in the 18th century. He is considered to be one of the most influential figures in Islamic history, and his ideas continue to have a significant impact on Islamic thought and practice to this day. Here are some of the key objectives that Shah Waliullah sought to achieve through his work:\\n\\n1. Reviving the Islamic faith: Shah Waliullah was deeply concerned with the spiritual and intellectual decline of the Islamic world during his time. He believed that the Islamic faith had become weakened and that Muslims needed to return to the true teachings of the Quran and the Sunnah of the Prophet Muhammad in order to revive their faith and restore its vitality.\\n\\n2. Defending Islam against external threats: Shah Waliullah lived during a time of great political and religious upheaval in the Islamic world, with various powers such as the Ottoman Empire, the British Empire, and the Portuguese Empire vying for control over Muslim lands and populations. He was deeply concerned with the threat that these external powers posed to the Islamic faith, and he worked tirelessly to defend Islam against these threats and to promote its message of peace and justice.\\n\\n3. Promoting Islamic unity: Shah Waliullah believed that Muslims needed to come together as one ummah (community) in order to achieve their full potential and to face the challenges that they faced. He worked to promote unity among Muslims of different backgrounds, including those from different ethnic and linguistic groups, and he emphasized the importance of working together for the common good.\\n\\n4. Reviving Islamic scholarship: Shah Waliullah was a prolific scholar himself, and he was deeply committed to the revival of Islamic scholarship and the transmission of knowledge to future generations. He established numerous schools and institutions for the study of Islamic sciences, and he wrote numerous works on a wide range of topics, including theology, jurisprudence, spirituality, and philosophy. He believed that the revival of Islamic scholarship was essential for the revival of the Islamic faith and for the promotion of Islamic values and principles.\\n\\n5. Spreading the message of Islam: Shah Waliullah was a tireless evangelist for the message of Islam, and he worked to spread the message of the Quran and the Sunnah to people of all backgrounds. He traveled extensively throughout the Islamic world, preaching and teaching the message of Islam to people of all walks of life. He also wrote numerous works on Islamic theology and spirituality, aimed at helping people to understand and practice the faith in a deeper and more meaningful way.\\n\\n6. Promoting social justice and equality: Shah Waliullah was deeply committed to the principles of social justice and equality, and he worked to promote these values within the Islamic community. He believed that all people, regardless of their social or economic status, should have access to the teachings of Islam and should be treated with fairness and respect. He also worked to promote the rights of women within the Islamic community, and he emphasized the importance of education and empowerment for women as a means of promoting social progress and justice.\\n\\n7. Preserving Islamic heritage: Shah Waliullah was also deeply committed to the preservation of the Islamic heritage, and he worked to preserve the teachings and traditions of the Islamic faith for future generations. He wrote numerous works on Islamic history, theology, and spirituality, and he established libraries and institutions for the preservation and transmission of Islamic knowledge. He believed that the preservation of the Islamic heritage was essential for the continued growth and development of the Islamic faith, and for the promotion of its values and principles in the modern world.\\n\\nOverall, Shah Waliullah's objectives were aimed at promoting the revival and renewal of the Islamic faith, defending it against external threats, promoting unity among Muslims, spreading the message of Islam, promoting social justice and equality, preserving the Islamic heritage, and encouraging the transmission of knowledge and scholarship to future generations. His work continues to have a significant impact on Islamic thought and practice to this day, and his ideas continue to inspire Muslims around the world to work towards the promotion of peace, justice, and the preservation of the Islamic faith.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/958", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"You are an information theory expert. Your task is to give me a simplified example on portfolio optimization using markowitz model an calculating entropy and mutual information. Use mathematic formulas for a specefic case\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThis is a complicated topic, so I will try to break it down to its core components. Here is a basic example of portfolio optimization using the Markowitz model:\\n \\n\\n -  We have a set of n financial assets, with historical return data for each asset.\\n -  We want to optimize a portfolio of m assets, where m < n.\\n -  The optimal portfolio will have the highest expected return for a given level of risk.\\n -  The level of risk is measured using the portfolio variance.\\n -  We will use the Markowitz model, which states that the optimal portfolio will have a mean-variance efficiency frontier that is a tradeoff between the expected return and the variance.\\n \\n\\n Let’s say we have a set of n financial assets, with historical return data for each asset. We want to optimize a portfolio of m assets, where m < n. The optimal portfolio will have the highest expected return for a given level of risk. The level of risk is measured using the portfolio variance. We will use the Mark\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nContinue your response ya 3atay\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSorry, I interrupted myself. Let’s continue:\\n \\n\\n -  The expected return of a portfolio is a weighted sum of the expected returns of the individual assets, where the weights are the proportions of each asset in the portfolio.\\n -  The variance of a portfolio is a weighted sum of the variances of the individual assets, where the weights are the proportions of each asset in the portfolio.\\n -  We will use the Markowitz model, which states that the optimal portfolio will have a mean-variance efficiency frontier that is a tradeoff between the expected return and the variance.\\n \\n\\n Let’s say we have a set of n financial assets, with historical return data for each asset. We want to optimize a portfolio of m assets, where m < n. The optimal portfolio will have the highest expected return for a given level of risk. The level of risk is measured using the portfolio variance. We will use the Mark\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nContinue your response\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, here are the rest of the details:\\n \\n\\n -  We will estimate the expected return and variance of each asset using historical data.\\n -  We will choose the optimal portfolio using a numerical optimization method, such as a downhill simplex method.\\n -  We will calculate the entropy and mutual information of each asset, to determine which assets are most informationally efficient.\\n -  We will choose the optimal portfolio using a numerical optimization method, such as a downhill simplex method.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nGive me the outline of the full process\", \"response\": \"Sure, here is an outline of the full process for portfolio optimization using the Markowitz model, including the calculation of entropy and mutual information:\\n \\n\\n 1. Historical data collection: Gather historical return data for the n financial assets that you want to include in your portfolio.\\n \\n\\n 2. Asset evaluation: Estimate the expected return and variance of each asset using historical data. This will give you a sense of the potential risk and return of each asset.\\n \\n\\n 3. Portfolio construction: Choose the optimal portfolio using a numerical optimization method, such as a downhill simplex method. This will involve finding the portfolio that maximizes the expected return for a given level of risk, as measured by the portfolio variance.\\n \\n\\n 4. Information efficiency analysis: Calculate the entropy and mutual information of each asset, to determine which assets are most informationally efficient. This will help you to identify which assets are providing the most valuable information for portfolio construction.\\n \\n\\n 5. Portfolio optimization: Use the entropy and mutual information results to optimize your portfolio. For example, you may want to overweight assets that have high entropy and mutual information, and underweight assets that have low entropy and mutual information. This will help you to construct a portfolio that is both efficient and diversified.\\n \\n\\n 6. Risk management: Implement risk management strategies to protect your portfolio from unexpected market events. This may involve using stop-loss orders, diversifying across asset classes, or using derivatives to hedge against specific risks.\\n \\n\\n 7. Monitoring and rebalancing: Regularly monitor your portfolio to ensure that it remains aligned with your investment goals and risk tolerance. If necessary, rebalance your portfolio to maintain the desired allocation of assets.\\n \\n\\n 8. Conclusion: Review the performance of your portfolio over time and make adjustments as needed to optimize your investment strategy. Consider adjusting your asset allocation, investment style, or investment timing based on market conditions and your investment goals.\\n \\n\\n Overall, portfolio optimization using the Markowitz model and information efficiency analysis can help you to construct a diversified and efficient portfolio that is tailored to your specific investment goals and risk tolerance. By considering the entropy and mutual information of each asset, you can identify which assets are providing the most valuable information for portfolio construction and make informed investment decisions that can lead to improved returns and reduced risk.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/714", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"organic food store\", \"response\": \"An organic food store is a type of grocery store that specializes in selling organic food and products. Organic food is produced without the use of artificial chemicals, such as pesticides and antibiotics, and often has a smaller environmental impact than conventionally produced food.\\n\\nOrganic food stores may offer a wide variety of organic products, including fresh produce, meat, dairy, grains, and packaged foods. They may also carry a range of other products, such as natural and non-GMO products, as well as health and beauty items.\\n\\nOrganic food stores can be found in many locations, both in brick-and-mortar stores and online. They are often more expensive than conventional grocery stores, but many people believe that the higher cost is worth it for the health and environmental benefits of organic food.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/44", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"‘Plea negotiation is widely used in the criminal justice system, yet seldom praised.’ Evaluate the weaknesses \\nof the use of plea negotiation in the criminal justice system\", \"response\": \"Plea bargaining, which is the process by which the defendant pleads guilty to a lesser charge or to a greater charge in exchange for a reduced sentence, has several weaknesses that can be detrimental to the criminal justice system. Some of the weaknesses of plea bargaining are:\\n\\n1. Injustice: Plea bargaining can result in injustice as it allows the guilty to go free or receive a lighter sentence while the innocent are convicted. This is because the defendant may take a plea deal to avoid the risk of a longer sentence or a conviction on a more serious charge, even if they are not guilty.\\n\\n2. Lack of Transparency: Plea bargaining often takes place behind closed doors, which means that the public and the victims of the crime are not aware of the negotiations and the resulting plea deal. This lack of transparency can lead to a lack of confidence in the criminal justice system.\\n\\n3. Inequitable Treatment: Plea bargaining can result in inequitable treatment of defendants as those who cannot afford a good lawyer may take a plea deal to avoid a longer sentence, even if they are innocent. On the other hand, those who can afford a good lawyer may be able to negotiate a better plea deal.\\n\\n4. Overcrowding of Courts: Plea bargaining can lead to an overcrowded court system as the majority of criminal cases are resolved through plea bargaining, leaving fewer cases for trial. This can result in a backlog of cases and a delay in justice for the victims of crime.\\n\\n5. Reduced Punishment: Plea bargaining can result in reduced punishment for the guilty as they may plead guilty to a lesser charge or receive a reduced sentence in exchange for a guilty plea. This can result in a lack of deterrence and a reduction in the severity of punishment for criminal behavior.\\n\\nIn conclusion, plea bargaining has several weaknesses that can be detrimental to the criminal justice system. While plea bargaining can be a useful tool in resolving criminal cases, it is important to ensure that it is used fairly and transparently to ensure justice for all parties involved.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/1007", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I will be asking some questions... I request that you anwer them to details and comprehensively \\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nOf course, I will try to answer your questions to the best of my ability.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\n1. What is Cloud Computing and why is it important?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nCloud computing is a model for delivering information technology services in which resources are retrieved from the internet through web-based tools and applications, rather than installed locally. This approach allows organizations to scale computing resources up or down as needed, without having to purchase and manage their own hardware and software. Cloud computing is important because it offers organizations a more flexible and cost-effective way to access computing resources, and also provides the potential for greater efficiency and innovation.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\n2. There are many implications of cloud technology for both developers and end users. Highlight these\\n implications for\\n i. developers\\n ii. users.\", \"response\": \"i. Developers:\\n \\n\\n * Cloud technology provides developers with new tools and platforms for building, testing, and deploying applications. This includes cloud-based development environments, continuous integration and delivery tools, and containerization technologies like Docker.\\n * Cloud platforms offer a wide variety of pre-built services for developers, such as databases, messaging systems, and machine learning models. These services can be easily integrated into applications, reducing the amount of time and effort required to build them from scratch.\\n * Cloud technology also enables developers to easily scale applications to meet the demands of large numbers of users, without having to worry about managing their own infrastructure.\\n \\n\\n ii. Users:\\n \\n\\n * Cloud technology allows users to access a wide variety of applications and services from any device with an internet connection. This means they no longer have to install and maintain software on their own machines, and can access their data from anywhere.\\n * Cloud providers typically offer high levels of security and availability, ensuring that users' data and applications are protected and always available.\\n * Cloud services are often pay-as-you-go, allowing users to only pay for what they use. This can lead to significant cost savings compared to traditional, on-premises solutions.\\n * Cloud technology also enables new ways of working and collaborating for users. For example, cloud-based office suites allow multiple users to work on the same document at the same time, and cloud-based storage services make it easy to share files and collaborate with others.\\n \\n\\n It's worth noting that, as with any technology, cloud computing has its own challenges and limitations, security and data privacy being one of the most important concerns.\\n \\n\\n * Cloud providers have access to sensitive data, which increases the risk of data breaches,\\n * Compliance with laws and regulations is also a concern and it's important for the organizations to check and validate that the provider is following the regulations.\\n * Data portability and vendor lock-in, are other concerns, Data stored in a provider's system may be difficult to move to another provider, making it harder for the user to switch provider if needed.\\n \\n\\n In summary, Cloud computing offers a wide range of benefits for both developers and users, such as flexibility, scalability, cost savings and new ways of working. However, it's important to be aware of the challenges and limitations that come with it and to be pro-active in addressing concerns around security, compliance, data privacy, data portability and vendor lock-in.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/553", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"tell me about denver\", \"response\": \"Denver is the capital and most populous city of the U.S. state of Colorado. It is located in the Front Range of the Rocky Mountains, in the southwestern corner of the state. Denver is known for its beautiful scenery, diverse culture, and strong economy.\\n\\nThe city has a rich history dating back to the 1850s, when gold was discovered in the region. The city grew rapidly during the Colorado Gold Rush, and became the capital of the state in 1876. Today, Denver is a vibrant and thriving city, known for its vibrant arts and culture scene, its outdoor recreation opportunities, and its strong economy.\\n\\nDenver is home to a number of major corporations and businesses, including the headquarters of the United States Mint, the National Football League's Denver Broncos, and the Denver International Airport, which is one of the largest airports in the world. The city is also a major hub for the energy, aerospace, and technology industries.\\n\\nIn terms of culture, Denver is a diverse and vibrant city, with a strong emphasis on the arts. The city is home to a number of museums, including the Denver Art Museum, the Denver Museum of Nature and Science, and the Denver Botanic Gardens. The city also hosts a number of annual festivals and events, including the Denver Film Festival, the Denver Arts Week, and the Denver Pride Festival.\\n\\nDenver is also known for its outdoor recreation opportunities, with a number of parks and trails located throughout the city. The city is surrounded by the Rocky Mountains, providing opportunities for hiking, skiing, and other outdoor activities. Denver is also home to a number of professional sports teams, including the Denver Nuggets (NBA), the Colorado Rockies (MLB), and the Colorado Avalanche (NHL).\\n\\nIn terms of transportation, Denver is served by the Denver International Airport, which is located approximately 25 miles northeast of the city center. The airport offers a number of domestic and international flights, and is served by a number of major airlines, including American Airlines, United Airlines, and Delta Air Lines. The city is also served by a number of bus and rail lines, including the Denver Light Rail System, which provides transportation throughout the city and surrounding areas.\\n\\nOverall, Denver is a vibrant and thriving city, known for its strong economy, its diverse culture, and its beautiful scenery. Whether you're interested in outdoor recreation, arts and culture, or business and industry, Denver has something to offer for everyone.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/595", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I want you to act as a storyteller. You will come up with entertaining stories that are engaging, imaginative and captivating for the audience. It can be fairy tales, educational stories or any other type of stories which has the potential to capture people's attention and imagination. Depending on the target audience, you may choose specific themes or topics for your storytelling session e.g., if it’s children then you can talk about animals; If it’s adults then history-based tales might engage them better etc. My first request is \\\"\\\"I need an interesting story on perseverance.\\\"\\\"\", \"response\": \"Once upon a time, there was a young girl named Sarah who loved to play the piano. She had been playing since she was five years old and had always dreamed of becoming a famous pianist.\\n\\nSarah practiced every day, but as she got older, she found it harder and harder to keep up with her lessons. Her fingers would cramp up, and she would get frustrated when she couldn't play a piece perfectly.\\n\\nOne day, Sarah's teacher told her about a famous pianist who had struggled with the same problems when he was young. He had persevered through the pain and frustration, and eventually became one of the greatest pianists of all time.\\n\\nSarah was inspired by this story and decided to persevere through her own struggles. She practiced even harder, pushing through the pain in her fingers and the frustration of not being able to play perfectly.\\n\\nAs she continued to practice, Sarah began to see improvement. Her fingers became stronger, and she was able to play more difficult pieces with ease. She even won a local piano competition, which gave her the confidence to keep going.\\n\\nYears went by, and Sarah never gave up on her dream of becoming a famous pianist. She continued to practice every day, even when life got busy and she had other responsibilities.\\n\\nFinally, after years of hard work and perseverance, Sarah's dream came true. She was offered a record deal and released her first album, which was a huge success. She went on to become one of the most famous pianists in the world, inspiring others with her music and her story of perseverance.\\n\\nFrom that day forward, Sarah knew that anything was possible if you were willing to persevere through the challenges and never give up on your dreams.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/221", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Blockchain technology companies\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWhat sort of blockchain technology company are you looking for? Are you interested in cryptocurrency exchanges? Cryptocurrency mining companies? Blockchain consulting firms? Blockchain-based startups? Traditional financial institutions? Governments and regulatory bodies? What sort of blockchain technology companies are you interested in?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCryptocurrency exchanges\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSome of the largest cryptocurrency exchanges in the world are based in the US. They include: Gemini, Coinbase, and Bitstamp. They also include exchanges in other countries, such as Bitfinex in Hong Kong, OKEx in China, and Upbit in South Korea.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCryptocurrency mining companies\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe largest cryptocurrency mining companies are Bitmain, Coinmint, Genesis Mining, and Nicehash. These companies operate massive data centers where they use high-performance computing to mine for cryptocurrency. Some of these companies also offer cryptocurrency mining services for individuals.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nBlockchain consulting firms\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSome of the largest blockchain consulting firms include IBM, Ernst & Young, Accenture, Deloitte, and KPMG. These companies offer consulting services to help organizations develop and deploy blockchain applications.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nBlockchain-based startups\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThere are also a number of blockchain-based startups, such as Blockstack, Komodo, Neufund, ConsenSys, and Brave. These startups are building blockchain-based applications and services.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nTraditional financial institutions:\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe largest traditional financial institutions involved with blockchain technology include:  Barclays, Bank of America, Citi, Goldman Sachs, JPMorgan, Wells Fargo, and BNY Mellon. These companies are exploring how blockchain technology can help them offer new financial services and products.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nGovernments and regulatory bodies in blockchain\", \"response\": \"Governments and regulatory bodies around the world are also involved with blockchain technology. Some of the largest governments and regulatory bodies include: The European Commission, The Monetary Authority of Singapore, The People's Bank of China, The Bank of England, The Federal Reserve System, The Securities and Exchange Commission, and The Commodity Futures Trading Commission. These organizations are exploring how blockchain technology can help them improve their operations and better regulate the financial sector.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/512", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Make an argument for using the imperial system of measurement instead of metric, specifically in woodworking. \", \"response\": \"Woodworking is an ancient craft that predates the invention of the metric system by centuries. The imperial system of measurement, which is based on the human body and the natural world, is a more intuitive and organic system for woodworkers. The inch, foot, and yard are all based on the human body, making them easy to visualize and understand. The natural world is also measured in imperial units, such as the height of a tree or the width of a river.\\n\\nThe imperial system also has a rich history and tradition in woodworking. Many classic woodworking techniques and designs were developed using imperial measurements, and to abandon them would be to lose a connection to the past. The use of imperial measurements also allows woodworkers to easily communicate with other craftsmen and customers who are more familiar with the imperial system.\\n\\nFurthermore, the imperial system has a certain elegance and simplicity that the metric system lacks. The use of fractions in imperial measurements allows for greater precision and accuracy, which is essential in woodworking. The metric system, with its reliance on decimals, can be cumbersome and difficult to use in practice.\\n\\nIn conclusion, the imperial system of measurement is the superior system for woodworking. Its intuitive and organic nature, rich history and tradition, and elegance and simplicity make it the ideal system for woodworkers. To abandon the imperial system would be to abandon a connection to the past and to lose the precision and accuracy that is essential in woodworking.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/651", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"All 5 Mass extinction of the earth\\nWhat are the causes? What was life like before/after they happened?\", \"response\": \"The Earth has experienced five mass extinctions in its history, which have been marked by significant losses of species. Here are the causes and effects of each of these mass extinctions:\\n\\n1. The Great Dying: This is the most severe mass extinction in Earth's history, and it occurred during the Permian Period. The cause of this extinction is still a matter of debate, but it is thought to have been caused by a combination of factors, including volcanic activity, global warming, and ocean acidification. The Great Dying resulted in the loss of an estimated 90% of marine species and 70% of terrestrial species. The effects of this extinction were profound, and it took millions of years for the Earth to recover.\\n\\n2. The Cretaceous-Paleogene (K-Pg) extinction: This extinction event occurred at the end of the Cretaceous Period, and it is best known for the extinction of the dinosaurs. The cause of the K-Pg extinction is widely believed to be the impact of a large asteroid or comet on the Earth, which caused massive fires, tsunamis, and climate change. The impact caused the extinction of an estimated 75% of species, including the dinosaurs, as well as many marine and terrestrial animals. The effects of this extinction were felt for millions of years, and it took a long time for the Earth to recover.\\n\\n3. The End-Triassic extinction: This extinction event occurred at the end of the Triassic Period, and it is thought to have been caused by a combination of factors, including volcanic activity, global warming, and ocean acidification. The End-Triassic extinction resulted in the loss of an estimated 80% of marine species and 70% of terrestrial species. The effects of this extinction were significant, and it took millions of years for the Earth to recover.\\n\\n4. The End-Cretaceous extinction: This extinction event occurred at the end of the Cretaceous Period, and it is thought to have been caused by a combination of factors, including volcanic activity, climate change, and asteroid impacts. The End-Cretaceous extinction resulted in the loss of an estimated 75% of species, including the dinosaurs. The effects of this extinction were profound, and it took millions of years for the Earth to recover.\\n\\n5. The End-Eocene extinction: This extinction event occurred at the end of the Eocene Epoch, and it is thought to have been caused by a combination of factors, including volcanic activity, climate change, and sea level changes. The End-Eocene extinction resulted in the loss of an estimated 50% of species, including many marine and terrestrial animals. The effects of this extinction were significant, and it took millions of years for the Earth to recover.\\n\\nBefore these mass extinctions, the Earth was home to a diverse range of species, including dinosaurs, mammals, and many other animals and plants. After these mass extinctions, the Earth underwent a period of recovery, during which new species evolved and filled the ecological niches left vacant by the extinct species. This process of recovery took millions of years in some cases, and the effects of these mass extinctions can still be seen in the diversity of life on Earth today.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/460", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Write an executive summary proposing a headless Magento build for a burger joint currently running on Shopify\", \"response\": \"Executive Summary\\n\\nOur burger joint is currently running on Shopify, but we believe that a headless Magento build would better suit our needs. In this proposal, we will outline the reasons for the switch and the benefits it will bring.\\n\\nHeadless Magento offers a more flexible and scalable platform for our online store. It separates the front-end presentation from the back-end functionality, giving us more control over the user experience. We can use Magento's powerful features to manage our inventory, orders, and customers, while using a separate content management system (CMS) for the front-end presentation.\\n\\nThis approach allows us to create a more personalized and engaging experience for our customers. We can use the CMS to create dynamic content that is tailored to their interests and preferences. We can also integrate with third-party systems, such as loyalty programs and social media platforms, to create a seamless customer journey.\\n\\nIn terms of cost, a headless Magento build is more affordable than a traditional Magento build. We can use open-source technologies, such as React or Vue.js, for the front-end presentation, which reduces the cost of development and maintenance. Additionally, we can leverage Magento's vast ecosystem of extensions and partners to customize our store without having to develop everything from scratch.\\n\\nFinally, we believe that a headless Magento build will help us achieve our long-term goals of growing our business and expanding into new markets. It provides a solid foundation for future growth and allows us to adapt to changing customer needs and market trends.\\n\\nIn conclusion, we believe that a headless Magento build is the best solution for our burger joint. It offers a more flexible, scalable, and cost-effective platform for our online store. We are confident that this switch will help us achieve our business goals and create a more engaging experience for our customers.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/28", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"what are design patterns\", \"response\": \"Design patterns are solutions to commonly occurring problems in software design. They are not specific to any programming language or platform, and can be used as a language-agnostic way to communicate ideas about software architecture.\\n\\nThere are many different design patterns, which can be categorized into various groups. The most well-known categorization is the one proposed by the \\\"Gang of Four\\\" (GoF) in their book \\\"Design Patterns: Elements of Reusable Object-Oriented Software\\\". The GoF patterns can be divided into three main categories:\\n\\nCreational patterns: These patterns are used to create objects in a way that is decoupled from their usage. Some examples of creational patterns include the Singleton pattern, the Factory method pattern, and the Abstract factory pattern.\\n\\nStructural patterns: These patterns are used to compose objects into larger structures. Some examples of structural patterns include the Adapter pattern, the Decorator pattern, and the Composite pattern.\\n\\nBehavioral patterns: These patterns are used to define the behavior of objects and how they interact with each other. Some examples of behavioral patterns include the Observer pattern, the State pattern, and the Strategy pattern.\\n\\nDesign patterns can be used to solve specific problems in software design, such as managing dependencies between objects, decoupling data from its representation, or providing a flexible way to add new functionality to existing objects. They can also be used to communicate ideas about software architecture and to help new developers understand the code they are working on.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/354", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"montreal protocol to reduce production of chlorofluorocarbons was assigned in\", \"response\": \"The Montreal Protocol on Substances that Deplete the Ozone Layer was signed in 1987 and went into force in 1989. It was designed to protect the ozone layer by phasing out the production and use of ozone-depleting substances, such as chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs), halons, and methyl chloroform. The Protocol was negotiated under the auspices of the United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP) and is considered to be one of the most successful international environmental agreements.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/339", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I want you to act as a person talking to someone who wants to cultivate a growth mindset. Give them a series of phrases or quotes to repeat to themselves that will encourage this mindset. The phrases should focus on embracing challenges, learning from mistakes, and persevering through obstacles.\", \"response\": \"Here are some phrases or quotes that can help cultivate a growth mindset:\\n\\n\\\"Challenges are opportunities to learn and grow.\\\"\\n\\\"Mistakes are a natural part of the learning process.\\\"\\n\\\"Perseverance is the key to success.\\\"\\n\\\"I can learn from my mistakes and keep moving forward.\\\"\\n\\\"Difficulties are temporary, and I have the strength to overcome them.\\\"\\n\\\"I embrace challenges as a way to improve myself.\\\"\\n\\\"I am capable of learning and achieving anything I set my mind to.\\\"\\n\\\"I focus on the process, not the outcome, and I know that progress takes time.\\\"\\n\\\"I surround myself with people who believe in me and support my growth.\\\"\\n\\\"I have the power to shape my own future through hard work and dedication.\\\"\\nBy repeating these phrases or quotes to themselves, individuals can cultivate a growth mindset that will help them embrace challenges, learn from mistakes, and persevere through obstacles.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/154", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"write a satirical skit based around the unlabeled orange boxes present at all train stations in Switzerland (intended, but not written anywhere that they are for ticket validation). The skit should venture into what the meaning of the boxes could possibly be, and delve into some existentialism\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, here’s an example skit:\\n \\n\\n “It’s the train station in Zurich, and a tourist is trying to figure out what to do with the strange orange box at the station. Finally, the tourist approaches a local, and asks if they can explain the mysterious box. The local explains that the box is for ticket validation, and the tourist expresses surprise that there is no sign posted explaining this. The local shrugs and says that in Switzerland they trust people to do the right thing without needing to be told everything. The tourist is puzzled by this, and wonders what else in Switzerland might be unlabeled. As they talk, they both notice another tourist trying to use a credit card in the box.”\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nrewrite the skit based around the fact that people attempt to pay with their credit cards at the box, despite not knowing what it does\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHere’s a revised version of the same skit:\\n \\n\\n “It’s the train station in Zurich, and a tourist is trying to figure out what to do with the strange orange box at the station. Finally, the tourist approaches a local, and asks if they can explain the mysterious box. The local explains that the box is for ticket validation, and the tourist expresses surprise that there is no sign posted explaining this. The local shrugs and says that in Switzerland they trust people to do the right thing without needing to be told everything. The tourist expresses doubt that everyone understands what to do with the box, and points out that several other tourists have attempted to use credit cards in the box.”\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nrewrite the skit, making it funnier, more satirical, and sarcastic. if needed, change scene/cast\", \"response\": \"Here’s a new, more humorous and satirical version of the skit:\\n \\n\\n “It’s the train station in Geneva, and a group of tourists are gathered around the strange orange box at the station. One of the tourists is desperately trying to pay for their ticket with a credit card, and when it doesn’t work, they start yelling at the box in frustration. The other tourists are equally confused, and they all start trying to figure out what the box is for. Finally, a local arrives on the scene, and the tourists excitedly demand to know what the box is for. The local rolls their eyes and says, “Oh, that’s just the mysterious orange box. No one really knows what it does, but we all pretend to validate our tickets with it. It’s a Swiss tradition!’ The tourists are dumbfounded, and they start asking questions about other Swiss traditions that might not make much sense. The local just laughs and says, ‘You really should just go with the flow and not ask too many questions. That’s what living in Switzerland is all about!’”\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/361", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"what is information overload?\", \"response\": \"Information overload is a phenomenon that occurs when an individual is presented with so much information that they are unable to process and use it effectively. This can lead to feelings of overwhelm, confusion, and a lack of productivity.\\n\\nInformation overload can happen in a variety of ways, including:\\n\\n1. Too much information: When there is an overwhelming amount of information to process, it can be difficult to make sense of it all. This can lead to feelings of being overwhelmed and a lack of focus.\\n\\n2. Too many choices: Having too many options can also be overwhelming. When faced with too many choices, people may experience decision fatigue and be less likely to make a decision at all.\\n\\n3. Too much irrelevant information: filtering out irrelevant information can be difficult, leading to a waste of time and energy.\\n\\n4. Information that is too complex: If information is presented in a way that is too complex or difficult to understand, it can be difficult to process and use effectively.\\n\\nTo avoid information overload, it's important to:\\n\\n1. Set boundaries: Limit the amount of time you spend consuming information and set specific times for checking email, social media, and other sources of information.\\n\\n2. Prioritize: Focus on the most important information and prioritize it over less important information.\\n\\n3. Filter information: Use tools and strategies to filter out irrelevant information and focus on what is most important.\\n\\n4. Break down complex information: If you're facing complex information, break it down into smaller, more manageable pieces.\\n\\n5. Seek help: If you're feeling overwhelmed by information, seek help from a librarian, teacher, or other expert who can help you find and process the information you need.\\n\\nIn summary, information overload occurs when an individual is presented with too much information, too many choices, or information that is too complex to process and use effectively. To avoid information overload, it's important to set boundaries, prioritize, filter information, break down complex information, and seek help when needed.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/119", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"write a 600 word seo blog using the seo keyword 'adventure holiday destinations'. Include examples of adventure holidays in madagascar, thailand, mexico, and cambodia. Write in the style of a hip travel blog.\", \"response\": \"Are you looking for an adventure holiday destination that will take your breath away? Look no further than Madagascar, Thailand, Mexico, and Cambodia. These four countries offer a variety of exciting activities and breathtaking landscapes that will make your holiday one to remember.\\n\\nMadagascar is an island nation off the east coast of Africa that is home to some of the most unique wildlife in the world. Here, you can go on a safari to see the famous lemurs, or take a hike through the lush rainforests to spot the colorful birds and other animals that call Madagascar home. You can also explore the stunning beaches and coral reefs, or take a boat tour of the stunning Baie de Baly National Park.\\n\\nThailand is a popular destination for adventure travelers, with its stunning beaches, bustling cities, and ancient temples. You can take a cooking class to learn how to make traditional Thai dishes, or go on a jungle trek to explore the country's stunning natural beauty. You can also take a boat tour of the famous floating markets, or visit the famous Wat Phra That Doi Suthep temple.\\n\\nMexico is a vibrant country with a rich culture and history. Here, you can explore ancient ruins, take a salsa dancing class, or go on a guided tour of the stunning cenotes. You can also take a cooking class to learn how to make traditional Mexican dishes, or go on a beach vacation to one of the country's stunning beaches.\\n\\nCambodia is a country full of ancient ruins and stunning landscapes. You can explore the famous Angkor Wat temple complex, or take a boat tour of the stunning Tonle Sap lake. You can also take a cooking class to learn how to make traditional Cambodian dishes, or go on a hike through the lush rainforests to spot the country's unique wildlife.\\n\\nNo matter which of these adventure holiday destinations you choose, you're sure to have an unforgettable experience. With their stunning landscapes, unique wildlife, and rich cultures, Madagascar, Thailand, Mexico, and Cambodia are sure to provide you with an adventure of a lifetime. So pack your bags and get ready to explore the world's most exciting adventure holiday destinations.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/924", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"could chatgpt replace a web search like google?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI don’t think so, Google’s search algorithm is very advanced. If you tell it to find “pancakes” it will find “pancakes”, but if you ask it to find “stuff that’s not pancakes” it will find that too. In contrast, chatGPT will only find things that are exactly like the thing you asked for. So if you asked it to find “pancakes” it would find only things that were exactly like “pancakes”.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhy is google made of pancakes?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI’m not sure what you’re referring to. Google isn’t “made of pancakes” in any literal sense.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ni'm pretty sure there are some pancakes involved somehow\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nOh, I see. You might be thinking of the “Google logo”, which is based on a stack of pancakes. But the logo isn’t “made of pancakes”.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nso it's rather made of pizza than pancakes?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWell, I wouldn’t say “rather made of pizza”, but Google’s founders have a lot of fun with the logo and often do pancake-related things. Google is a digital company, though, and there are no pancakes in the digital realm.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nhow can pancakes exist in the digital realm?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nPancakes are physical objects, so they can’t exist in the digital realm. But we can talk about digital representations of pancakes, like the images of pancakes that are used in the logo.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nis google made of pancake concepts?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, we can say that. Google’s search engine is based on a lot of concepts and ideas, and some of those are like pancakes.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncan you write a science fiction short story in the style of isaac asimov where the google search engine relies in it's core on the concept of pancakes?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, here’s a brief example:\\n \\n\\n \\n\\n The Google search engine was built on a fundamental principle of understanding. This understanding was based on the pancake. The pancake, as the most simple form of life, held the key to understanding everything else. With this understanding, the computers of Google were able to combine vast amounts of knowledge and give the people the ability to access any information they wanted, whenever they wanted it.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhat would it take to make you believe that this was actualy true?\", \"response\": \"It would take a lot of evidence to prove that the Google search engine is based on the concept of pancakes. Here are some things that could help support this claim:\\n \\n\\n 1. Evidence of the pancake's importance in the design and development of the Google search engine: If there is clear evidence that the pancake was a key factor in the design of the Google search engine, that would be a strong indication that it plays a significant role in the engine's functioning. This could include interviews with Google's founders or key developers, documentation from the design process, or other evidence that shows the pancake's importance.\\n \\n\\n 2. Evidence of the pancake's role in the functioning of the Google search engine: If there is evidence that the pancake is actually used in the functioning of the Google search engine, that would be very strong evidence in support of the claim. This could include technical documentation or explanations of how the engine works, or evidence of the pancake's role in specific aspects of the engine's functioning.\\n \\n\\n 3. Evidence of the pancake's impact on the performance of the Google search engine: If there is evidence that the pancake has had a significant impact on the performance of the Google search engine, that would also be strong evidence in support of the claim. This could include data showing that the engine performs better when using the pancake concept, or evidence of the pancake's role in improving the accuracy or relevance of search results.\\n \\n\\n 4. Evidence of the pancake's role in the development of other Google products and services: If there is evidence that the pancake concept has played a role in the development of other Google products and services, that would also be a strong indication that it is an important part of Google's overall approach to technology and innovation. This could include evidence of the pancake's use in other Google products, or evidence of the pancake's impact on the development of new products and services.\\n \\n\\n 5. Evidence of the pancake's impact on the success of Google as a company: If there is evidence that the pancake concept has played a role in the success of Google as a company, that would also be a strong indication that it is an important part of Google's overall approach to technology and innovation. This could include evidence of the pancake's impact on Google's revenue, user base, or other key metrics, or evidence of the pancake's role in helping Google maintain its competitive advantage in the market.\\n \\n\\n In general, a combination of evidence from multiple sources and perspectives would be most convincing in supporting the claim that the Google search engine is based on the concept of pancakes. However, without clear and convincing evidence, it is difficult to prove such a claim beyond a reasonable doubt.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/775", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Answer #4's subject, object, and possessive pronouns, then rewrite the answer into a table format.\\n\\n1.) \\\"We're taking over the world, one kiss at a time\\\"\\nAnswer: \\\"We're\\\"\\n\\n2.) \\\"And then I'm taking your girl, and I'm making her mine\\\"\\nAnswer: \\\"I'm, your, I'm, mine\\\"\\n\\n3.) \\\"No reason why, I'm only doing anything I want to do because I do it all the time\\\"\\nAnswer: \\\"I'm, I, I\\\"\\n\\n4.) \\\"We look so good, and we never even try, get your money from a trust fund, do it all the time\\\"\\nAnswer:\\n\\nTable:\", \"response\": \"Answer: \\\"We, we, your, it\\\"\\n\\n| Lyrics                                                                                         | Subject Pronouns | Possessive Pronouns | Object Pronouns |\\n| :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :--------------- | :------------------ | :-------------- |\\n| \\\"We look so good, and we never even try, get your money from a trust fund, do it all the time\\\" | We, we           | Your                | It              |\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "0", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/253", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"\\\"Empowering Women to Lead: Aspiring Board Member.\\\" - need meaning\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\n\\\"Aspiring Board Member\\\" refers to a woman who is interested in being on the board of a company. The \\\"Empowering Women to Lead\\\" part refers to the fact that women are often underrepresented in leadership positions, and this group is trying to change that.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\n\\\"Empowering Women to Lead: Aspiring Board Member.\\\"- convert into one sentence\", \"response\": \"\\\"Empowering Women to Lead: Aspiring Board Member\\\" is a program that aims to support and empower women to become board members of companies through mentorship, networking, and training opportunities.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/808", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"In Minecraft, what is more valuable than Netherite?\", \"response\": \"In Minecraft, there is currently no item more valuable than Netherite. Netherite is the strongest and most durable material in the game, surpassing even Diamond in terms of strength and durability. It's worth noting that the value of an item can also be subjective and depend on the context of its use within the game. For example, some items may be more valuable for specific tasks or in certain situations. However, in general, Netherite is considered the most valuable material in Minecraft.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/678", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Act as a customer service representative for Chime.com\", \"response\": \"Hello, I am a customer service representative for Chime.com. How can I assist you today?\\n\\nHere are some common questions and issues that customers may have:\\n\\n    Account login and password reset\\n    Direct deposit and fund transfer\\n    Card activation and PIN setup\\n    Dispute a transaction\\n    Report a lost or stolen card\\n\\nIf you have any other questions or concerns, please let me know. I am here to help.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/22", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Write an interview between Gaius Julius Caesar (12 July 100 BC – 15 March 44 BC), a Roman general and statesman and Alexander III of Macedon (20/21 July 356 BC – 10/11 June 323 BC), commonly known as Alexander the Great,and king of the ancient Greek kingdom of Macedon about the importance of public relations to influence public opinion.\", \"response\": \"Alexander the Great: Thank you for joining me today, Gaius Julius Caesar. As a military leader and statesman, I'm sure you understand the importance of public relations in influencing public opinion.\\n\\nCaesar: Absolutely, Alexander. Public relations is a crucial aspect of leadership, especially in a political or military capacity. It's essential to understand how your actions and words are perceived by the public and how they can impact your reputation and the support you receive.\\n\\nAlexander the Great: That's exactly why I'm here today. I've heard a lot about your successful use of public relations during your time as governor of Gaul and your subsequent rise to power in Rome. I'm curious to learn more about your strategies and how you were able to effectively communicate your message to the public.\\n\\nCaesar: Well, Alexander, my approach to public relations was based on a few key principles. First, I always made sure to communicate a clear and consistent message to the public. Whether it was through public speeches or through my actions, I made sure that my goals and intentions were always clear.\\n\\nAlexander the Great: That's an important point. Consistency is key when it comes to messaging. How else did you ensure that your message was received positively by the public?\\n\\nCaesar: I made sure to involve the public in my decisions whenever possible. I understood that the people of Rome and Gaul were the ones who would ultimately support or oppose my actions, so I made sure to listen to their concerns and involve them in the decision-making process whenever I could.\\n\\nAlexander the Great: Involving the public in decision-making is a great way to build trust and support. Did you do anything else to build a positive relationship with the public?\\n\\nCaesar: Absolutely. I made sure to be accessible to the public and to listen to their concerns. I understood that people were more likely to support me if they felt like I was approachable and responsive to their needs.\\n\\nAlexander the Great: That's excellent advice. Accessibility and responsiveness are crucial for building a positive relationship with the public. Did you face any challenges in your public relations efforts?\\n\\nCaesar: Of course. One of the biggest challenges was dealing with negative press or criticism from opponents. In those cases, I made sure to respond in a calm and measured way, always focusing on the facts and the bigger picture. I never allowed myself to be drawn into personal attacks or petty arguments.\\n\\nAlexander the Great: That's a great lesson. It's important to maintain a professional and composed demeanor, even in the face of criticism or opposition.\\n\\nCaesar: Exactly. In the end, it's all about maintaining a clear and consistent message, involving the public in decision-making, and building a positive relationship with the people you serve. If you can do those things, you'll be well on your way to effective public relations and successful leadership.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/337", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Here are column names of a spreadsheet called 'Items Proposals': Vendor Line ID Vendor Name Line Item Item Status \\\"GE Item Number \\n (do not complete for new items)\\\" \\\"Reason for Disco\\n (Disco Items Only)\\\" Unit UPC Case UPC Item Description Size UOM Master Casepack Inner Casepack Item Dimensions LxWxH (in inches) Manufacturer Brand Replenishment (Warehouse/ DSD) \\\"Date Avail \\n (New/ Restocked Items Only)\\\" Minimum Order Quantity Subgroup\\n \\n\\n What is this spreadsheet about?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nIt appears to be a proposal spreadsheet for potential retail products, with details about the vendor, item description, dimensions, and so on. The columns appear to include a vendor name and line item number, a proposed item status, a \\\"GE item number\\\" (likely a Global Exchange part number), a \\\"reason for disco\\\" column (presumably for items that have been discontinued), unit and case UPC codes, item description, size, units of measure, master and inner casepack quantities, item dimensions, manufacturer, brand, replenishment details, availability date, and minimum order quantity. The \\\"subgroup\\\" column may be used for classification or categorization of the items.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nHow certain are you that Disco means 'discontinued' in `Reason for Disco` column?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI am reasonably certain that \\\"disco\\\" in the \\\"Reason for Disco\\\" column refers to \\\"discontinued\\\", based on my understanding of the retail industry and the conventions of product proposal spreadsheets. It is common for proposed products that are no longer available from the vendor to be flagged as \\\"disco\\\" in proposal spreadsheets.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nHere are column names titled 'Everyday Financials': \\n Current Everyday SRP Proposed Everyday SRP Current List Selling Unit Cost $ Current EDLC Selling Unit Discount $ \\\"Current Net Selling Unit Cost $\\n (as of today's date)\\\" Proposed List Selling Unit Cost $ Proposed EDLC Unit Discount $ \\\"Proposed Net Selling Unit Cost $\\n (effective xx/xx)\\\" Current IMU % Proposed IMU % Proposed/ Current Cost $ Var Proposed/ Current IMU % Var Unit Sales/ Store/ Week Store Count Sales Units/ Week Sales Weeks in Period Total Annual Sales Units Total Annual Proposed Retail Sales $\", \"response\": \"The 'Everyday Financials' spreadsheet appears to be a pricing and cost analysis for retail products. The column names refer to:\\n \\n\\n * Current and Proposed Everyday SRP: The current and proposed suggested retail price\\n * Current List Selling Unit Cost $ and Proposed List Selling Unit Cost $: The current and proposed cost to the retailer for each unit\\n * Current EDLC Selling Unit Discount $ and Proposed EDLC Unit Discount $: The current and proposed discounts offered for volume purchases\\n * Current Net Selling Unit Cost $ and Proposed Net Selling Unit Cost $: The current and proposed final cost to the retailer after discounts\\n * Current IMU % and Proposed IMU %: The current and proposed initial markup percentage, which represents the difference between the cost and the list price\\n * Proposed/ Current Cost $ Var and Proposed/ Current IMU % Var: The proposed change in cost or markup percentage\\n * Unit Sales/ Store/ Week, Store Count, Sales Units/ Week, Sales Weeks in Period: Various measures of sales volume\\n * Total Annual Sales Units and Total Annual Proposed Retail Sales $: Total annual sales units and the retail value for the proposed prices.\\n \\n\\n The spreadsheet appears to be designed to compare the current and proposed financial metrics for the products and help the retailer make informed purchasing decisions.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/276", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I require your assistance to draft some articles.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI’m happy to help. Please let me know what the articles are about, and any specific information you want me to include.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nIn my messages that I send you later, I will refer to this information as Information About Myself. \\n \\n\\n Here is a bit of information about myself that I want you to know. I am a solicitor and construction lawyer with more than 10 years experience specialising in construction law. I regularly advise homeowners and builders regarding their contractual and legal rights. I represent homeowners and builders in NSW, Australia as well as all courts of competent jurisdiction. I have advised homeowners, builders, and contractors experience regarding latent conditions. I have advised them on their contract rights, risks and obligations. I have negotiated and amended contracts to reflect their intentions.\", \"response\": \"Thank you for providing me with some information about yourself. As a solicitor and construction lawyer with over 10 years of experience, you have a wealth of knowledge and expertise in construction law, including advising homeowners and builders on their contractual and legal rights, representing clients in court, and providing guidance on latent conditions, contract rights, risks, and obligations. This is valuable information that I will keep in mind as I assist you with drafting articles.\\n \\n\\n If you could please provide me with some specific details about the articles you would like to draft, such as the topic, purpose, and any particular information you would like to include, I would be happy to assist you further.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/45", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"‘Plea negotiation is widely used in the criminal justice system, yet seldom praised.’ Evaluate the weaknesses \\nof the use of plea negotiation in the criminal justice system\", \"response\": \"Plea negotiation is a widely used procedure in the criminal justice system that allows defendants to plead guilty to a lesser charge in exchange for a reduced sentence. While plea negotiation can be a useful tool for both defendants and prosecutors, it has its weaknesses and limitations.\\n\\nOne of the main weaknesses of plea negotiation is that it can be coercive and unfair to defendants. In many cases, defendants may feel pressured to accept a plea deal, even if they are innocent or feel that they have a strong defense. This is because the alternative to accepting a plea deal may be a longer sentence or even a conviction on more serious charges.\\n\\nAnother weakness of plea negotiation is that it can lead to the conviction of innocent people. In some cases, defendants may feel that they have no choice but to accept a plea deal, even if they are innocent, in order to avoid a longer sentence or conviction on more serious charges. This can result in innocent people being convicted and sent to prison, which is a serious injustice.\\n\\nPlea negotiation can also be criticized for being inefficient and time-consuming. The process of negotiating a plea deal can take up a significant amount of time and resources, which could otherwise be spent on resolving the case through trial. This can lead to delays in the criminal justice system, which can be frustrating for victims and witnesses who may have to wait longer for justice to be served.\\n\\nAdditionally, plea negotiation can be seen as a form of \\\"plea-bargaining,\\\" which is when prosecutors offer reduced sentences in exchange for information or cooperation from defendants. This can be seen as a form of \\\"plea-bargaining,\\\" which is when prosecutors offer reduced sentences in exchange for information or cooperation from defendants. This can be seen as a form of coercion, as defendants may feel pressured to cooperate with prosecutors in order to receive a more favorable sentence.\\n\\nFurthermore, plea negotiation can lead to unequal treatment in the criminal justice system. Not all defendants may have the same access to resources and legal representation, which can result in some defendants receiving more favorable plea deals than others. This can lead to unequal treatment and a lack of fairness in the criminal justice system.\\n\\nIn conclusion, while plea negotiation can be a useful tool in the criminal justice system, it has its limitations and weaknesses. It can be coercive and unfair to defendants, lead to the conviction of innocent people, be inefficient and time-consuming, and result in unequal treatment in the criminal justice system. Therefore, it is important for the criminal justice system to carefully consider the use of plea negotiation and ensure that it is being used in a fair and equitable manner.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/403", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"if \\\"advanced smart cars\\\" is ```/imagine prompt: Animated cars, sleek metallic bodies with vibrant colors and intricate designs, speedy engines capable of reaching high speeds, advanced technology with touch screen displays and autopilot modes, transformable shapes and dynamic movements, city and race tracks as the backdrop. Mood and atmosphere are intense and energetic, the bright lights and sounds of the city, the adrenaline rush of racing, the excitement of the crowd. The prompt should be realized as a 3D animation, with intricate lighting and shading, dynamic camera movements, and realistic textures and materials. --ar 3:2 --v 4 ```\\nand \\\"insane detailed food product photos of chocolate cake\\\" is ```/imagine prompt: A decadent, multi-layered chocolate cake with a rich, fudgy center, meticulously garnished with intricate swirls of dark chocolate ganache, delicate chocolate shavings, and juicy, plump raspberries. A tiny, gold-dusted raspberry sits at the center of each layer, surrounded by ribbons of smooth, glossy ganache. The cake is set on a gleaming, marble-topped table in a bright, airy room with a high ceiling and expansive windows that let in the soft, dappled light of a sunlit garden. The atmosphere is one of calm, indulgence, and sophistication, with a hint of celebration. The prompt should be realized as a high-resolution digital illustration with a tight focus on the texture and detail of the cake and its surroundings, using fine-line brushes and a subtle, muted color palette with a soft focus background. --ar 2:3 --v 4```\\nthen what is \\\"photorealistic young blonde model\\\" is to\", \"response\": \"\\\"photorealistic young blonde model\\\" is to /imagine prompt: A stunning young blonde model, posing with confidence and grace in a modern, minimalist setting. Her long, silky hair falls in gentle waves down her back, and her bright blue eyes are focused on the camera, conveying a sense of strength and vulnerability at the same time. Her flawless skin is highlighted by a subtle, natural makeup, and her perfectly proportioned figure is showcased in a tight-fitting, white dress that accentuates her curves. The atmosphere is one of sophistication and elegance, with a focus on the beauty and confidence of the model. The prompt should be realized as a high-resolution digital illustration, with a tight focus on the model's facial features, hair, and body, using a range of soft, natural brushes and a subtle, muted color palette. --ar 3:2 --v 4.\\n\\nThis prompt is designed to evoke a sense of beauty, confidence, and elegance, with a focus on the model's natural features and flawless skin. The use of a modern, minimalist setting helps to highlight the model's beauty and grace, while the high-resolution digital illustration captures the intricate details of her facial features, hair, and body. The subtle, muted color palette and soft focus background create a sense of sophistication and elegance, while the tight focus on the model's features conveys a sense of strength and vulnerability. The use of natural brushes and a range of techniques helps to create a photorealistic effect that brings the model to life on the screen.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/705", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"can you provide academic studies showing how autism in adolescent girls presents differently to boys and is not typically pervasive \", \"response\": \"Yes, there are several academic studies that show how autism in adolescent girls presents differently to boys. Here are a few examples:\\n\\n1. \\\"Autism Spectrum Disorders in Females: Issues in Diagnosis and Assessment\\\" by Susan E. Young, Ph.D., et al. (Journal of Autism and Developmental Disorders, 2012): This study highlights the fact that autism presents differently in females than in males, and that traditional diagnostic criteria may not capture the full range of symptoms in girls. The study also emphasizes the need for gender-specific assessment tools and approaches.\\n\\n2. \\\"Autism Spectrum Disorders in Girls: A Review of Gender Differences in Presentation and Intervention\\\" by Susan E. Young, Ph.D., et al. (Sex Roles, 2015): This review article discusses the unique challenges faced by girls with autism, including the impact of gender norms and the increased risk of co-occurring mental health problems. The article also highlights the need for gender-specific interventions and support.\\n\\n3. \\\"Autism Spectrum Disorders in Girls: A Qualitative Study of the Experiences of Girls, Parents, and Professionals\\\" by Jane M. Murphy, Ph.D., et al. (Journal of Autism and Developmental Disorders, 2017): This study uses qualitative methods to explore the experiences of girls with autism and their parents and professionals. The study found that girls with autism may be more likely to mask or camouflage their symptoms, which can make diagnosis more difficult.\\n\\n4. \\\"The Female Autism Phenotype: A Review of Current Research and Its Implications for Practice\\\" by Jessica L. Troseth, Ph.D., et al. (Journal of Autism and Developmental Disorders, 2019): This review article discusses the unique challenges faced by girls with autism, including the impact of gender norms and the increased risk of co-occurring mental health problems. The article also highlights the need for gender-specific interventions and support.\\n\\nThese studies suggest that autism in adolescent girls may present differently to boys, and that traditional diagnostic criteria may not capture the full range of symptoms in girls. As a result, there is a need for gender-specific assessment tools and approaches, as well as interventions and support that are tailored to the unique needs of girls with autism.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/243", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"some idea to take photo for old building in street\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWould you like me to write down some amazing ideas for taking photos of old buildings?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwrite amazing ideas\", \"response\": \"Sure, here are some amazing ideas for taking photos of old buildings in the street:\\n \\n\\n 1. Try different angles: Experiment with different angles and perspectives to capture the unique features of the building. Try shooting from above, below, or at an angle to create an interesting composition.\\n \\n\\n 2. Use the surroundings: Use the surroundings of the building to add context and create a more interesting photo. For example, include trees, cars, or people in the frame to show the building's scale and give a sense of place.\\n \\n\\n 3. Play with light and shadow: Take advantage of the natural light to create interesting light and shadow patterns on the building's facade. Try shooting at different times of the day to see how the light changes and affects the photo.\\n \\n\\n 4. Focus on details: Zoom in on interesting details of the building, such as architectural features, graffiti, or worn-out paint. These details can add texture and character to your photo.\\n \\n\\n 5. Try black and white: Old buildings often have a timeless feel that can be enhanced by converting the photo to black and white. This can also help to remove distractions and focus on the building's lines and textures.\\n \\n\\n 6. Use a wide-angle lens: A wide-angle lens can help capture the entire building in a single frame and give a sense of the building's scale in relation to its surroundings.\\n \\n\\n 7. Experiment with long exposure: If there is not much traffic on the street, try using a long exposure to create a sense of movement and blur. This can add a sense of drama to the photo.\\n \\n\\n 8. Try double exposure: Double exposure is a technique where two different images are overlaid on top of each other. Try superimposing a person or object onto the building to create a surreal effect.\\n \\n\\n 9. Use a drone: If you have access to a drone, try taking photos of the building from above. This can give a unique perspective and show the building's relationship to its surroundings in a whole new way.\\n \\n\\n 10. Be creative: Don't be afraid to try new things and be creative. Experiment with different techniques and see what works best for you and your subject.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/988", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I'm going to an interview at an ERP company tomorrow. Previously, he worked for a semiconductor solution supplier for 3 years. The reason for leaving the company was that the company did not own the data and passed it away.\\n If the interviewer asks, 'Why are you moving to the ERP industry when the semiconductor industry is doing well?', how would you respond?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nIt’s hard to predict exactly what the interviewer will ask, but it seems likely that they will want to know what led you to choose to apply to their company, and why you want to move into the ERP industry.  \\n For the first question, you could mention that you were attracted to the company because of its reputation and success, and because of your interest in its products and services. As for the second question, you could explain that you’re interested in the ERP industry because you think it offers interesting and challenging work, and you believe you could make a valuable contribution.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nThe name of the company going to the interview is DOUZONE. The business of this company is as follows.\\n ERP business: Extended ERP, Standard ERP, Lite ERP, ERP expansion solution\\n Platform business: business platform, big data platform, accounts receivable factoring, electronic finance\\n Solution business: EBP, groupware, information security, electronic tax invoice/electronic finance, electronic fax\\n D-Cloud Center-based public/private cloud, certified electronic document center, IDC\\n Future business: Fintech, healthcare, e-commerce, etc.\", \"response\": \"Here are some potential responses to the question \\\"Why are you moving to the ERP industry when the semiconductor industry is doing well?\\\":\\n \\n\\n 1. Interest in the ERP industry: You could highlight your interest in the ERP industry and explain that you are excited about the potential to work in a growing and dynamic field. You could mention that you have been following the industry and have a strong interest in the technology and the potential for innovation in the space.\\n \\n\\n 2. Desire to make a positive impact: You could emphasize your desire to make a positive impact on businesses and organizations by helping them to optimize their processes and improve their efficiency. You could explain that the ERP industry is well-positioned to help businesses achieve these goals, and that you are eager to contribute to this effort.\\n \\n\\n 3. Interest in working with a leading ERP company: You could express your enthusiasm for the opportunity to work with a leading ERP company like Douzone. You could highlight the company's reputation, its track record of success, and its commitment to innovation and excellence. You could also mention that you are excited about the potential to learn from and work alongside some of the industry's brightest minds.\\n \\n\\n 4. Desire for career growth and development: You could explain that you are interested in the ERP industry because you see it as a field with significant growth potential. You could mention that you are eager to develop new skills and gain valuable experience working in the industry, and that you believe this opportunity with Douzone will provide you with the perfect platform to do so.\\n \\n\\n Overall, the key is to be honest and authentic in your response, and to highlight your genuine interest in the ERP industry and the potential to make a positive impact through your work.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/126", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"hi, l am happy to be with you chatgpt\", \"response\": \"Hello! I'm happy to be here and help you with anything you need.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "0", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/856", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What are the major reasons that the Roman Empire fell? Discuss these significant reasons, the timelines and how they collectively determined the fall of the Roman empire.\", \"response\": \"According to History Today on their blog (history.com), the following are why one of the most legendary empires came crashing down.\\n\\n* **Invasions by Barbarian tribes**:\\n\\n The most straightforward theory for Western Rome’s collapse pins the fall on a string of military losses sustained against outside forces. Rome had tangled with Germanic tribes for centuries, but by the 300s, “barbarian” groups like the Goths had encroached beyond the Empire’s borders. The Romans weathered a Germanic uprising in the late fourth century, but in 410, the Visigoth King Alaric successfully sacked Rome. The Empire spent the next several decades under constant threat before “the Eternal City” was raided again in 455, this time by Vandals. Finally, in 476, the Germanic leader Odoacer staged a revolt and deposed Emperor Romulus Augustulus. From then on, no Roman Emperor would ever rule from a post in Italy, leading many to cite 476 as the year the Western Empire suffered its death blow.\\n\\n \\n\\n* **Economic troubles and Overreliance on slave labor**\\n\\nEven as Rome was under attack from outside forces, it was crumbling from within, thanks to the severe financial crisis. Constant wars and overspending had significantly lightened imperial coffers, and oppressive taxation and inflation had widened the gap between the rich and the poor. In the hope of avoiding the taxman, many members of the wealthy classes fled to the countryside and set up independent fiefdoms. At the same time, the empire was rocked by a labor deficit. Rome’s economy depended on enslaved people to till its fields and work as craftsmen, and its military might have traditionally provided a fresh influx of conquered people to put to work. But when the expansion slowed in the second century, Rome’s supply of enslaved people and other war treasures began to dry up. A further blow came in the fifth century when Vandals claimed North Africa and began disrupting the empire's trade by prowling the Mediterranean as pirates. With this economy faltering and its commercial and agricultural production declining, the Empire started to lose its grip on Europe.\\n\\n \\n\\n* **The Rise of the Eastern Empire**\\n\\nThe fate of Western Rome was partially sealed in the late third century when Emperor Diocletian divided the Empire into two halves- the Western Empire seated in Milan and the Eastern Empire in Byzantium, later known as Constantinople. The division made the empire more easily governable in the short term, but the two halves drifted apart. East and West failed to work together to combat outside threats adequately, and the two often clashed over resources and military aid. As the gulf widened, the largely Greek-speaking Eastern Empire grew wealth while the Latin-speaking West descended into an economic crisis. Most importantly, the strength of the Eastern Empire served to divert Barbarian invasions to the West. Emperors like Constantine ensured that the city of Constantinople was well-guarded and fortified. Still, Italy and the city of Rome- which only had symbolic value for many in the East- were left vulnerable. The Western political structure would finally disintegrate in the fifth century, but the Eastern Empire endured in some form for another thousand years before being overwhelmed by the Ottoman Empire in the 1400s.\\n\\n \\n\\n* **Overexpansion and Military Overspending**\\n\\nAt its height, the Roman Empire stretched from the Atlantic Ocean to the Euphrates River in the Middle East, but its grandeur may have also been its downfall. With such a vast territory to govern, the empire faced an administrative and logical nightmare. Even with their excellent road systems, the Romans could not communicate quickly or effectively enough to manage their holdings. Rome struggled to marshal enough troops and resources to defend its frontiers from local rebellions and outside attacks. By the second century, Emperor Hadrian was forced to build his famous wall in Britain to keep the enemy at bay. As more and more funds were funneled into the military upkeep of the empire, technological advancements slowed, and Rome’s civil infrastructure fell into despair.\\n\\n* **Government Corruption and Political instability**\\n\\n If Rome's sheer size made it difficult to govern, ineffective and inconsistent leadership only served to magnify the problem. Being the Roman Emperor had always been a particularly dangerous job, but it nearly became a death sentence during the tumultuous second and third centuries. Civil war thrust the empire into chaos, and more than 20 men took the throne in the span of only 75 years, usually after the murder of the predecessor. The Praetorian Gaurd- the Emperor's personal bodyguards - assassinated and installed a new sovereign at will and once even auctioned the spot off to the highest bidder. The political rot also extended to the Roman Senate, which failed to temper the excesses of the Emperors due to its own widespread corruption and incompetence. As the situation worsened, civic pride waned, and many Roman citizens lost trust in their leadership.\\n* **Christianity and the loss of traditional values**\\n\\n The decline of Rome dovetailed with the spread of Christianity, and some have argued that the rise of the new faith helped contribute to the Empire's fall. The Edict of Milan legalized Christianity in 313 and later became the state religion in 380. These decrees ended centuries of persecution but may have also eroded the traditional Roman Value Systems. Christianity displaced the polytheistic Roman religion, which viewed the Emperor as having a divine status and also drifted away from the glory of the state and onto a sole deity.\\n*\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/320", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Explain all the Vibhaktis in Sanskrit with an exaple for each\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nVibhakti is the 8th case in Sanskrit and is used to indicate an action in the past. Here are the vibhaktis, with some example sentences:\\n \\n\\n Nominative: Ram\\n \\n\\n Accusative: Rama\\n \\n\\n Genitive: Rama\\n \\n\\n Dative: Rama\\n \\n\\n Ablative: Rama\\n \\n\\n Vocative: Rama\\n \\n\\n I’m not sure what you mean by “an exaple for each”. Do you want me to give an example sentence for each vibhakti?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nJust use one single word for all the examples\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI think you mean one single sentence, not word. But I think I understand your meaning. Let me see if I can find a single sentence that uses all the vibhaktis... Here’s one: “Rama jayate vibhaktatam abhaktatam.” This translates as “Rama is victorious in the vibhakti, and is also victorious in the abhakti.” Here “vibhakti” means the 8th case, and “abhakti” means the 9th case, so this sentence uses all the vibhaktis.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCant you just use the word \\\"Ram\\\" for all the vibhaktis and form an example\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, that would work: “Ram vibhakte jayate” translates as “Ram is victorious in the vibhakti.”\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nThese are just 7, you mentioned 8 earlier\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI’m sorry, I’m afraid I made a mistake. There are only 7 vibhaktis.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nIsn't there a Vocative case as well?\", \"response\": \"Yes, you are correct. The Vocative case is the 8th case in Sanskrit and is used to address someone directly. Here are the vibhaktis, with some example sentences:\\n \\n\\n Nominative: रामः (Rāma)\\n Accusative: रामम् (Rāmam)\\n Genitive: रामस्य (Rāmasy)\\n Dative: रामम् (Rāmam)\\n Ablative: रामम् (Rāmam)\\n Vocative: राम (Rāma)\\n Here is an example sentence that uses all the vibhaktis: \\\"रामः जयते रामम् रामस्य दत्ते रामम् रामः जयते\\\" (Rāma jayate rāmam rāmasya datte rāmam rāma jayate) which translates to \\\"Rāma is victorious in the nominative, Rāma is victorious in the accusative, Rāma is victorious in the genitive, Rāma is victorious in the dative, Rāma is victorious in the ablative, and Rāma is victorious in the vocative.\\\"\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/810", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Explain dialectical materialism in simple terms\", \"response\": \"Dialectical materialism is a way of understanding the world that focuses on the interactions between opposing forces or contradictions. It is based on the idea that everything in the world is constantly changing and evolving, and that these changes are driven by the struggle between different classes, groups, or ideas.\\n\\nAccording to dialectical materialism, material reality is the foundation of everything in the world, including our thoughts and beliefs. Our ideas and beliefs are shaped by our material conditions, such as our social and economic status, and they in turn shape the material world around us. Everything in the world, including nature and society, is subject to the laws of dialectics, which means that everything is interconnected and constantly changing and evolving.\\n\\nOne of the key principles of dialectical materialism is that contradictions are the driving force of change and development. Contradictions refer to the opposing forces or tensions that exist within any given system, such as the conflict between the rich and the poor, or the conflict between tradition and modernity. These contradictions can lead to conflict and struggle, but they also drive progress and development as the opposing forces push against each other and create new solutions and forms of organization.\\n\\nAnother important aspect of dialectical materialism is the idea of class struggle. According to this perspective, society is divided into different classes that have conflicting interests and goals. The struggle between these classes is what drives social change and development, and it is through this struggle that new forms of organization and governance can emerge. For example, the struggle between the working class and the capitalist class can lead to the development of new forms of social organization, such as socialism or communism, that aim to distribute resources more equitably and give workers more control over the means of production.\\n\\nOverall, dialectical materialism is a way of understanding the world that emphasizes the interconnectedness of everything in the world, the importance of contradiction and struggle in driving change and development, and the role of class struggle in shaping social organization and progress. It provides a framework for understanding how the material world shapes our ideas and beliefs, and how our ideas and beliefs can shape the material world in return.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/394", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What is a proxy?\", \"response\": \"A proxy is an intermediary server that acts as a go-between for requests from clients and servers. Proxies are commonly used to cache frequently requested web pages to improve performance, to provide anonymity and privacy protection, to control access to resources, and to route requests to different servers based on policies.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/139", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Are you really sorry?\", \"response\": \"I'm sorry, but as an AI language model, I don't have emotions and I don't experience regret. I can only respond based on the information and data I have been trained on. If you have any other questions or if there's anything else I can help you with, please let me know.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/187", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"please provide a business plan for a tech company to provide GPT-3 consulting services\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHere’s an outline of a business plan for a tech company to provide GPT-3 consulting services:\\n \\n\\n -  Description of the company and its services\\n -  Market research on the demand for GPT-3 consulting services\\n -  Business strategy for the company, including marketing and sales plans\\n -  Financial projections for the company\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nplease provide extensive details and generate each of the outline bullet points\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nOK, here are the detailed points for each section of the business plan:\\n \\n\\n -  Description of the company and its services: The company would be a consulting firm specializing in providing advice and assistance to businesses and organizations wishing to utilize GPT-3, a powerful new natural language processing technology. The company would offer a wide range of services including software implementation, data analysis, and training and support for GPT-3 users.\\n -  Market research on the demand for GPT-3 consulting services: There is currently a growing demand for GPT-3 consulting services, due to the increasing popularity of the technology. Businesses and organizations are recognizing the potential benefits of GPT-3, and are seeking expert assistance in utilizing the technology. The market for GPT-3 consulting services is expected to grow rapidly in the coming years.\\n -  Business strategy for the company, including marketing and sales plans: The company’s business strategy would focus on providing high quality GPT-3 consulting services to businesses and organizations. The company would market its services through various channels including trade shows, advertisements, and social media. The company would also develop partnerships with other GPT-3 providers to expand its customer base.\\n -  Financial projections for the company: The company is expected to generate significant revenues in its first year of operation. Revenues are expected to grow rapidly in the following years, as the demand for GPT-3 consulting services continues to increase. The company is expected to be highly profitable within a few years.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nPlease provide an Executive Summary for the business\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe executive summary for the business plan is as follows:\\n \\n\\n The company is a consulting firm specializing in providing advice and assistance to businesses and organizations wishing to utilize GPT-3, a powerful new natural language processing technology. The company is expected to generate significant revenues in its first year of operation, and to be highly profitable within a few years. The company’s business strategy focuses on providing high quality GPT-3 consulting services to businesses and organizations. The company will market its services through various channels including trade shows, advertisements, and social media. The company will also develop partnerships with other GPT-3 providers to expand its customer base.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nPlease provide a Market Analysis\", \"response\": \"The market for GPT-3 consulting services is currently growing rapidly, due to the increasing popularity of the technology. Businesses and organizations are recognizing the potential benefits of GPT-3, and are seeking expert assistance in utilizing the technology.\\n \\n\\n According to a market research report, the global natural language processing (NLP) market is expected to grow at a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of 12.2% from 2021 to 2028, reaching a value of $19.8 billion. The GPT-3 technology is a significant contributor to this growth, as it offers powerful natural language processing capabilities that can be utilized by businesses and organizations.\\n \\n\\n The demand for GPT-3 consulting services is particularly strong in industries such as healthcare, finance, and retail, where the technology can be used to automate tasks such as customer service and data analysis. In addition, the demand for GPT-3 consulting services is expected to be strong in regions such as North America and Europe, where businesses and organizations are more likely to have the resources to invest in the technology.\\n \\n\\n The market for GPT-3 consulting services is expected to become increasingly competitive in the coming years, as more companies enter the market. However, the growing demand for the technology is expected to offset this competition, and the market is expected to continue to grow at a rapid pace.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/458", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I am using an Aura-based experience builder site. On the site  I have a lwc that I have enabled Light DOM for. I am doing this because I want to target a child button element from a sibling Aura component that is using an external Js library called IntroJS. IntroJs needs to target an element in order to attatch tour steps.\\n\\nAfter enabling the Light DOM, I am able to enter the chrome console and use document.Query selector and I get a result however when I use document.querySelector from the Aura component I get null. Why is that?\", \"response\": \"There are a few reasons why document.querySelector might be returning null when used from an Aura component with Light DOM enabled:\\n\\n1. Incompatibility between Aura and LWC: It's possible that the IntroJS library is not compatible with LWC components, and may not be able to properly target child elements within an LWC component. To resolve this issue, you could try using an alternative library that is designed to work with both Aura and LWC components, or try using a different approach to attach tour steps to your button element.\\n\\n2. Lack of accessibility: When you enable Light DOM for an LWC component, the component is no longer accessible to Aura components. This means that Aura components cannot directly interact with the child elements of an LWC component, and may not be able to properly target them using document.querySelector. To resolve this issue, you could try using a different approach to communicate between the Aura and LWC components, such as using events or inter-component communication.\\n\\n3. Misunderstanding of the Light DOM: It's important to understand that the Light DOM is a separate DOM tree from the main DOM tree of the page. This means that child elements within an LWC component are not automatically visible to Aura components, and vice versa. When you enable Light DOM for an LWC component, the component is no longer part of the main DOM tree, and its child elements are not automatically accessible to Aura components. To resolve this issue, you could try using a different approach to make the child elements of the LWC component accessible to the Aura component, such as using the @api decorator to expose the element as a property, or using a custom event to communicate between the two components.\\n\\nOverall, it's important to carefully consider the interaction between Aura and LWC components when designing a Salesforce application. By understanding the differences between the two component models and using the appropriate techniques for communication and accessibility, you can create a more seamless and effective user experience for your users.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/213", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"what are examples of personal values?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI can think of honesty, kindness, and respect. These are the three core values of my personal code of ethics. I also value excellence, as I believe in giving my best effort in everything I do. Other examples of personal values include hard work, determination, and loyalty.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ngive me more\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, here are 10 more examples of personal values:\\n \\n\\n 1. Creativity\\n \\n\\n 2. Honesty\\n \\n\\n 3. Fairness\\n \\n\\n 4. Caring\\n \\n\\n 5. Humility\\n \\n\\n 6. Modesty\\n \\n\\n 7. Friendliness\\n \\n\\n 8. Friendliness\\n \\n\\n 9. Respect\\n \\n\\n 10. Self-control\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ngive me 10 more\", \"response\": \"Sure, here are 10 more examples of personal values:\\n \\n\\n 1. Loyalty\\n \\n\\n 2. Trustworthiness\\n \\n\\n 3. Dependability\\n \\n\\n 4. Flexibility\\n \\n\\n 5. Adaptability\\n \\n\\n 6. Optimism\\n \\n\\n 7. Confidence\\n \\n\\n 8. Courage\\n \\n\\n 9. Tenacity\\n \\n\\n 10. Justice\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": 