{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/421", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"best methods to rich? 10\", \"response\": \"There are many ways to become wealthy, but here are 10 methods that can help:\\n\\n1. Create a budget and stick to it: A budget can help you track your spending and save money each month.\\n\\n2. Invest in stocks: Investing in stocks can help your money grow over time.\\n\\n3. Start a side hustle: A side hustle can be a great way to earn extra income.\\n\\n4. Cut back on unnecessary expenses: Reducing your spending on non-essential items can help you save money.\\n\\n5. Save money automatically: Set up automatic transfers from your checking account to a savings account each month.\\n\\n6. Invest in real estate: Investing in real estate can be a great way to build wealth over time.\\n\\n7. Get a raise: Negotiating a higher salary can help you increase your income.\\n\\n8. Pay off debt: Paying off debt can help you free up money each month to save and invest.\\n\\n9. Invest in yourself: Investing in your education and skills can help you increase your earning potential.\\n\\n10. Create multiple streams of income: Generating multiple streams of income can help you build wealth over time.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/46", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"\\nDhiWise is a automated code generator platform who is recently release Typescript feature, give some content for social media post\", \"response\": \"Here's a sample social media post you can use to promote the release of Typescript on DhiWise:\\n\\n\\\"Exciting news, developers! @DhiWise now supports Typescript, making it easier than ever to generate high-quality code for your projects. With Typescript, you can add type definitions to your code to improve its readability and maintainability. Try it out today and see how it can help you build better software faster! #Typescript #CodeGeneration #AutomatedCodeGeneration\\\"\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/759", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Adesewa is a 22-year-old lawyer who has 4 schools on her list of schools for a JD program. The first school, UNIBEN, has a minimum LSAT requirement score that is 8 times her age. The second school, UNIBAG, has a minimum LSAT requirement score of 160. For the third school, UNIORUN, the minimum LSAT requirement score is 10 more than UNIBAG's own. The last school, OSU, has a minimum LSAT requirement that is 5 more than UNIORUN's own. \\n\\nFrom the provided transcript, give me all the schools with a minimum LSAT score of 170 or more, arranging them in alphabetical order.\", \"response\": \"I'm sorry, I don't understand what you mean by \\\"provided transcript\\\". Can you please provide the transcript you are referring to?\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/586", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Heavyweight Laundry Use Case\\nUse Case 1\\tHousekeeper does laundry\\nActor\\tHousekeeper\\nUse Case Overview\\tIt is Wednesday and there is laundry in the laundry room. The housekeeper sorts it, then proceeds to launder each load. She folds the dry laundry as she removes it from the dryer. She irons those items that need ironing.\\nSubject Area\\tDomestics\\nActor(s)\\tThe housekeeper\\nTrigger\\tDirty laundry is transported to the laundry room on Wednesday.\\nPrecondition 1\\tIt is Wednesday\\nPrecondition 2\\tThere is laundry in the laundry room.\\nBasic Flow: Do Laundry\\nDescription\\tThis scenario describes the situation where only sorting, washing and folding are required. This is the main success scenario.\\n1\\tHousekeeper sorts laundry items.\\n2\\tHousekeeper washes each load.\\n3\\tHousekeeper dries each load.\\n4\\tHousekeeper verifies that laundry item does not need ironing, is clean and not shrunken.\\n5\\tHousekeeper verifies that laundry item is foldable.\\n6\\tHousekeeper folds laundry item\\n7\\tHousekeeper does this until there are no more laundry items to fold\\nTermination outcome\\tLaundry is clean and folded\\nAlternative Flow 4A: Laundry item needs ironing.\\nDescription\\tThis scenario describes the situation where one or more items need ironing before or in lieu of folding\\n4A1\\tHousekeeper verifies that the laundry item needs ironing and is clean and not shrunken\\n4A2\\tHousekeeper irons the laundry item\\n4A3\\tHousekeeper puts laundry item on a hanger\\nTermination outcome\\tLaundry that needs ironing is ironed and hung up.\\nAlternative flow 4B: Laundry item is dirty.\\nDescription\\tThis scenario describes the situation where the laundry item did not get clean the first time through the wash.\\n4B1\\tHousekeeper verifies that the laundry item is not clean.\\n4B2\\tHousekeeper rewashes the laundry item\\nTermination outcome\\tDirty laundry is rewashed.\\nAlternative flow 4C: Laundry item shrank.\\nDescription\\tThis scenario describes the situation where the laundry item shrank.\\n4C1\\tHousekeeper verifies that the laundry item shrank\\n4C2\\tHousekeeper disposes of laundry item.\\nTermination outcome\\tLaundry item no longer exists.\\nAlternative flow 5A: Laundry item needs hanger.\\nDescription\\tThis scenario describes the situation where the laundry item needs to be hung instead of folded.\\n5A1\\tHousekeeper verifies that laundry item needs hanging.\\n5A2\\tHousekeeper puts laundry item on a hanger.\\nTermination outcome\\tLaundry that needs hanging is hung up.\\nPost conditions: All laundry clean and folded or hung up.\\nBusiness Rules:\\n•\\tLaundry can only be done on Wednesdays.\\n•\\tAll ironed laundry items get hung on hangers\\n•\\tAny laundry item that is irrevocably soiled, shrunken, scorched, etc. , gets thrown out.\\n\\n\\nKeeping this in mind, can you give a heavyweight use case for an ATM Machine\", \"response\": \"Use Case: Withdraw Cash\\n\\nActors: Bank Customer\\n\\nUse Case Overview: A bank customer wants to withdraw cash from their account using an ATM machine. The customer inserts their bank card into the machine, enters their PIN, and selects the amount of cash they wish to withdraw. The ATM verifies the account has sufficient funds, dispenses the cash, and prints a receipt.\\n\\nSubject Area: Banking\\n\\nActor(s): The bank customer\\n\\nTrigger: The customer needs cash and approaches an ATM machine.\\n\\nPreconditions:\\n\\n1. The customer has a valid bank card.\\n2. The customer knows their PIN.\\n3. The ATM machine is operational and has sufficient cash.\\n\\nBasic Flow: Withdraw Cash\\n\\n1. The customer inserts their bank card into the ATM machine.\\n2. The customer enters their PIN.\\n3. The customer selects the amount of cash they wish to withdraw.\\n4. The ATM machine verifies the account has sufficient funds.\\n5. The ATM machine dispenses the cash.\\n6. The ATM machine prints a receipt.\\n7. The customer takes their bank card, cash, and receipt.\\n\\nTermination outcome: Cash is withdrawn successfully.\\n\\nAlternative Flow 6A: Insufficient funds.\\n\\nDescription: This scenario describes the situation where the customer's account does not have sufficient funds to cover the withdrawal.\\n\\n6A1. The ATM machine verifies that the account has insufficient funds.\\n6A2. The ATM machine displays a message indicating that the account has insufficient funds.\\n6A3. The ATM machine prompts the customer to enter a lower amount or cancel the transaction.\\nTermination outcome: The customer cancels the transaction or withdraws a lower amount.\\n\\nAlternative Flow 7A: ATM machine runs out of cash.\\n\\nDescription: This scenario describes the situation where the ATM machine runs out of cash during the transaction.\\n\\n7A1. The ATM machine verifies that it has run out of cash.\\n7A2. The ATM machine displays a message indicating that it has run out of cash.\\n7A3. The ATM machine prompts the customer to cancel the transaction or try again later.\\nTermination outcome: The customer cancels the transaction or tries again later.\\n\\nPost conditions: The customer has withdrawn cash or cancelled the transaction.\\n\\nBusiness Rules:\\n\\n* The customer must insert a valid bank card and enter the correct PIN.\\n* The customer's account must have sufficient funds to cover the withdrawal.\\n* The customer can only withdraw cash in whole dollar amounts.\\n* The ATM machine must have enough cash to dispense the requested amount.\\n* The customer must take their bank card, cash, and receipt before leaving the ATM machine.\\n* If the customer does not take their bank card, the ATM machine will retain it for security reasons.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/855", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I am preparing graphical movie summaries on my website. My first target is Disney's \\\"Tinker Bell.\\\" What are the different pixie fairies and their powers in the movie? In the lists, suggest a color theme that matches each fairy's outfit.\", \"response\": \"In the Tinker Bell movie, there are several pixie fairies, each with their own unique abilities and color themes:\\n\\n1. Tinker Bell (Tink) - Tink is a tinker fairy who specializes in fixing things and creating inventions. Her color theme is light green and yellow, which matches her outfit and her personality.\\n\\n2. Silvermist - Silvermist is a water fairy who can control water and create mist. Her color theme is light blue and white, which matches her outfit and her gentle personality.\\n\\n3. Rosetta - Rosetta is a garden fairy who can make plants grow and bloom. Her color theme is pink and green, which matches her outfit and her love of flowers.\\n\\n4. Iridessa - Iridessa is a light fairy who can create and control light. Her color theme is yellow and orange, which matches her outfit and her sunny personality.\\n\\n5. Fawn - Fawn is an animal fairy who can communicate with animals. Her color theme is brown and green, which matches her outfit and her love of nature.\\n\\n6. Vidia - Vidia is a fast-flying fairy who can create powerful gusts of wind. Her color theme is dark green and purple, which matches her outfit and her fierce personality.\\n\\n7. Clank and Bobble - Clank and Bobble are two tinker fairies who work with Tink. Their color theme is silver and gold, which matches their metalworking abilities and their quirky personalities.\\n\\nThese are the main pixie fairies in the Tinker Bell movie, each with their own unique abilities and color themes that match their personalities and outfits.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/315", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"We're working with the Welsh govt on the issue of Welsh language transmission from parent to child. They have ambitions to increase the number of Welsh speakers, and see intergenerational Welsh language transmission as playing a crucial role. We have an idea to develop a digital evaluation tool for parents which also becomes a nudge to encourage the behaviour. I'd love to get your initial thoughts on the idea. \\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nAbsolutely! Sounds great. Would you like me to just give you my best initial thoughts, or would you like me to act as an behavioral science research advisor and help create a detailed intervention process for this idea?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nI want you to act as an behavioral science research advisor. Your task is to help create a detailed intervention process for this idea. You should use your knowledge of behavioral science and psychology to create an effective step-by-step intervention strategy.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nGot it. Here's a process for designing the intervention:\\n \\n\\n 1. Explain the goal of the intervention.\\n 2. Determine the target behavior.\\n 3. Map the target behavior onto the COM-B model.\\n 4. Determine the main barriers to the target behavior.\\n 5. Create an effective intervention strategy.\\n 6. Evaluate the intervention.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nIn addition, you should include the 8 most important behavioral research questions to explore to succeed with the intervention.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nAbsolutely. Here are those eight questions:\\n \\n\\n 1. What is the current level of the target behavior?\\n 2. What are the key barriers to the target behavior?\\n 3. What factors enable the target behavior?\\n 4. What are the key contextual factors that affect the target behavior?\\n 5. What are the key psychological factors that affect the target behavior?\\n 6. What are the key social factors that affect the target behavior?\\n 7. What are the key structural factors that affect the target behavior?\\n 8. What are the key environmental factors that affect the target behavior?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nProvide suggested answers to the first four questions in the form of bullet points (three for each question). No need to repeat questions.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHere are three suggestions for answers to the first four questions:\\n \\n\\n 1. Current level of target behavior: Currently less than 50% of children in Wales are Welsh-speaking. This is the current baseline for the intervention.\\n 2. Key barriers to the target behavior: Low levels of parental support for the Welsh language, a lack of exposure to Welsh as a child, and a lack of training for parents in how to use Welsh with their children.\\n 3. Key enabling factors: Training for parents in how to use Welsh with their children, and the availability of Welsh-language resources.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nDo the same for the remaining questions\", \"response\": \"Here are three suggestions for answers to the remaining questions:\\n \\n\\n 5. Key psychological factors that affect the target behavior:\\n \\n\\n  - Attitudes towards the Welsh language and its use.\\n  - Self-efficacy in using Welsh with children.\\n  - Motivation to use Welsh with children.\\n \\n\\n 6. Key social factors that affect the target behavior:\\n \\n\\n  - Social norms around the use of Welsh.\\n  - Social support for using Welsh with children.\\n  - The influence of family and friends on language use.\\n \\n\\n 7. Key structural factors that affect the target behavior:\\n \\n\\n  - Availability of Welsh-language resources and services.\\n  - Access to Welsh-language education.\\n  - Policies and initiatives that support the use of Welsh.\\n \\n\\n 8. Key environmental factors that affect the target behavior:\\n \\n\\n  - The physical environment, such as the availability of Welsh-speaking communities.\\n  - The cultural environment, such as the presence of Welsh cultural events and activities.\\n  - The media environment, such as the availability of Welsh-language media.\\n \\n\\n Answering these questions will help you better understand the factors that affect the target behavior and inform the design of the intervention.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/93", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What are the exact words that the Queen says to her mirror in the 1937 film \\\"Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs\\\"?\", \"response\": \"In the 1937 film \\\"Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs,\\\" the Queen approaches her magic mirror and says, \\\"Magic mirror on the wall, who is the fairest one of all?\\\" The mirror responds, \\\"Your Majesty, you are the fairest one of all.\\\" Snow White, who is listening nearby, then steps forward and says, \\\"Excuse me, but I believe I am the fairest one of all.\\\" The Queen is taken aback and says, \\\"What? How dare you! Who are you?\\\" Snow White introduces herself and the Queen says, \\\"You, my dear, are the fairest one of all. You have surpassed me in beauty.\\\" Snow White then asks the Queen if she can stay with the seven dwarves, to which the Queen replies, \\\"Of course, my dear. You are welcome to stay with them. They will keep you safe and sound.\\\" The Queen then leaves, and Snow White is embraced by the seven dwarves.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/20", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Oldest living person\", \"response\": \"The current oldest living person is Kane Tanaka, a Japanese woman born on January 2, 1903. She is recognized by Guinness World Records as the oldest living person at the age of 119 years and 41 days as of April 2023.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/5", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"This is a set of ballots for a ranked choice election. Of a number is given before a line, there are that many identical ballots (otherwise, just one)\\na: Kiss\\nb: Montroll\\nc: Simpson\\nd: Smith\\ne: Wright\\nf: w-i\\n------------\\n840:e\\n355:a>b\\n326:a\\n271:e>d\\n256:e>b\\n234:a>b>d\\n200:b>a\\n178:b\\n147:e>b>d\\n145:b>a>d\\n139:b>d\\n125:a>d\\n124:d\\n33:a>b>d>e>c\\n2:e>d>b\\na>d>b\\na>b>d>c>\", \"response\": \"Here are the results of the ranked choice election based on the ballots provided:\\n\\n1st Round:\\n\\nKiss: 326 + 125 + 147 = 698 votes\\nMontroll: 355 + 200 + 178 = 733 votes\\nSimpson: 0 votes\\nSmith: 271 + 145 + 139 = 555 votes\\nWright: 256 + 234 + 124 = 614 votes\\nw-i: 33 votes\\n2nd Round:\\n\\nKiss: 698 votes\\nMontroll: 733 votes\\nSimpson: 0 votes\\nSmith: 555 votes\\nWright: 614 votes\\nw-i: 33 votes\\n3rd Round:\\n\\nKiss: 698 votes\\nMontroll: 733 votes\\nSimpson: 0 votes\\nSmith: 555 votes\\nWright: 614 votes\\nw-i: 33 votes\\n4th Round:\\n\\nKiss: 698 votes\\nMontroll: 733 votes\\nSimpson: 0 votes\\nSmith: 555 votes\\nWright: 614 votes\\nw-i: 33 votes\\nFinal Round:\\n\\nKiss: 698 votes\\nMontroll: 733 votes\\nSimpson: 0 votes\\nSmith: 555 votes\\nWright: 614 votes\\nw-i: 33 votes\\nBased on the final round, Kiss is the winner of the election with 698 votes, Montroll is the runner-up with 733 votes, Simpson received 0 votes, Smith received 555 votes, Wright received 614 votes, and w-i received 33 votes.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/940", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What's a list of non-existant substances or states of matter or energy? They could be obsolete or descredited science (pseudoscience), mytholgical or folkloric, or fictional. Phlogiston, chi, adamantium, mithril, aether, miasma are examples.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI think you're probably looking for an answer that's a bit more science-focused, but since you asked, I think I understand what you're looking for. A lot of pseud